     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (immediate-release, labeled maximum), and a dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis. A single 1,700 mg dose is also above the usual maximum for one administration, which is 850 mg to 1,000 mg.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- Another dose. Please tell me the intended dose and frequency.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, please confirm and add the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first. Once you reply, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
